<!-- Lumia 930 (martini). WCD9320 (Taiko) codec on SLIMbus and TI TAS2552
     loudspeaker amplifier (BLSP1 QUP5, I2C 0x40, enable PM8941 GPIO20) on
     the secondary MI2S, as on the Lumia 1520 (bandit), whose paths these
     are. Never tried on a 930.

     Why the 1520 routes apply: the stock RM-1045 firmware describes the
     audio hardware exactly as the 1520 one. The ADSP, codec, MBHC and QCRT
     ACPI tables are identical, the codec driver binary is the same, and the
     930 calibration (ACDB, DEVICE.SOC_QC8974.MARTINI) maps every device to
     the same codec path as the 1520 one (only the tuning data differs):
       - earpiece: EAR (HANDSET_SPKR, ACDB 7 -> EAROUT_SPEAKER)
       - headset: HPHL/HPHR (HEADSET_SPKR_STEREO, ACDB 10); headset mic on
         ADC2 with MIC BIAS2 (HEADSET_MIC, ACDB 8 -> ADC_2)
       - handset mic: ACDB 4 -> DMIC_1; speakerphone mic: ACDB 11 -> DMIC_4;
         broadside DMIC_1_2, endfire DMIC_2_4, camera DMIC_1_2_3_4 (four
         digital mics)
       - loudspeaker: SEC_MI2S_RX (ACDB 70), not a codec output; see the
         "sec-mi2s" paths and the "spk" path
     The 930 microphones are not those of the 1520: measured on an RM-1045
     (14/11/2026) with speech held as in a call, 3 s per codec DMIC at 0 dB:
     DMIC2 -73 dBFS RMS (peak -47), DMIC1 -80 (peak -63), DMIC3/DMIC4 only
     noise (-96), DMIC5/DMIC6 zero. Main and speakerphone mic DMIC2, second
     mic of the dual-mic paths DMIC1, both with +12 dB of decimator gain
     (DEC Volume 96, 84 = 0 dB).

     Vibra: the 930 drives its motor through the codec (stock
     hwnvibraaudiocodec); "vibra-lineout" is a test path for that route,
     not used by the HAL. No other path may use LINEOUT2/LINEOUT4.

     Original 1520 notes: based on the OnePlus One (bacon, LineageOS
     android_device_oneplus_bacon 7a4af4b), which has the same codec and
     msm8974-taiko sound card. -->
